Brackish Bloom

A reborn form of alternative rock where reggae-ska movement carries sharp melodic confession, while roots-psychedelic instrumentation keeps the performance organic, vulnerable, and unpredictable.

Fusion Formula: Ska-reggae punk × confessional alternative rock × rootsy psychedelic jam rock × adult reckoning × melodic bass — Experimental

Creative Philosophy

Brackish Bloom preserves the central contradiction shared by the three influences: the music feels liberating while the story reveals damage beneath the freedom.

This is not frozen 1990s nostalgia. The reckless protagonists have grown older. They now face custody arrangements, recovery, aging parents, unstable work, damaged friendships, and the consequences left behind by their younger selves. Freedom no longer means escape; it means remaining present when leaving would be easier.

